<title>USA: McDonald &amp; Co lists 1997 stock picks.</title>
<headline>McDonald &amp; Co lists 1997 stock picks.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald &amp; Co Investments Inc said on Tuesday it included AMP Inc, a maker of electronic connection devices, and credit card issuer Capital One Financial Corp and 10 other stocks in an annual list of stock recommendations.</p>
<p>&quot;Our goal is to identify well-run companies whose businesses we understand,&quot; Bradley Turner, senior managing director of McDonald's Gradison-McDonald Asset Management unit, said at a lunch speech unveiling his selections.</p>
<p>Last year's 12-stock list provided a 21.7 percent return, he said, adding he looks for consistent performance.</p>
<p>Tire maker Cooper Tire and Rubber Co, farm equipment maker Deere &amp; Co, energy firm Enron Corp, Hospitality Properties Trust, a hotel real estate investment trust, and home health care product maker Invacare Corp were also included.</p>
<p>Newell Co, which makes consumer hardware and housewares, food and beverage firm PepsiCo Inc, book and magazine publisher Reader's Digest Association Inc, hair salon chain Regis Corp and cellular phone firm SBC Communications Inc were also included.</p>
<p>((Cleveland Newsdesk, Susan Zimmerman 216-579-0077))</p>
